    "reasoning": "All 16 selected values agree with their own captured worked solutions. Coefficient comparison gives n+d=-20 and t=-3. The graphs give f'(-3)=-4/3 and g'(-3)=0, hence h'(-3)=4. Completing the square gives -3(y-1)^2+4 and 1/4-(y+9/2)^2. Implicit differentiation gives the four displayed derivative choices below; for q-108655, divide numerator and denominator by 3. The tangent slopes are -1 and 2\\sqrt{3}. For xy=5, the tangent at (1,5) is y=-5x+10, so P=(0,10). The four trigonometric expressions simplify using sin²+cos²=1; q-43288 equals 1 wherever its original denominators are nonzero. There is one authored premise error: q-2289 has no real points because y-2^y<0 for every real y, whereas 3x²≥0. Its selected formula is the correct formal differentiation result and matches MA, but it cannot describe a derivative of a real curve satisfying that equation. Thus the batch has a source error without a disagreement about the selected formal answer values. No prior submitted answers or grades were supplied.",
